;; BIND zone file for mashuphost.tech
;; Import via Cloudflare: DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import
;;
;; Import with "Proxy imported DNS records" UNCHECKED, then turn the orange cloud ON
;; for the six web hosts only. Final state:
;;
;;   PROXIED (orange)   @  www  admin  app  wifi  portal
;;   DNS ONLY (grey)    api  *
;;
;; Why api stays grey: Safaricom POSTs M-Pesa callbacks to it, and Cloudflare's Bot Fight
;; Mode / WAF can challenge non-browser POSTs. A challenged callback means the customer has
;; paid and the invoice stays open -- a silent failure on the payment path.
;; Why * stays grey: proxied wildcard records are an Enterprise-plan feature; on Free the
;; wildcard only works DNS-only.
;;
;; The proxied hosts need Cloudflare SSL/TLS mode = "Full (strict)". On "Flexible" Cloudflare
;; talks HTTP to the origin, Caddy redirects to HTTPS, and the result is a redirect loop.
;; The Caddyfile reads CF-Connecting-IP on those hosts so request.ip is the real visitor.
;;
;; TTL 1 means "Automatic" in Cloudflare.
;; Target: Azure VM mashuphost-vm, resource group mashuphost-rg (static public IP).
;; Re-check the address after any VM rebuild:
;;   az vm show -d -g mashuphost-rg -n mashuphost-vm --query publicIps -o tsv

mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
www.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
api.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
app.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
admin.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
wifi.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
portal.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
*.mashuphost.tech.		1	IN	A	68.210.187.104
